Okay, the fourth level (lower quest filler) was pretty interesting.
It had actual monsters in it, and it was genuinely different from
the other levels, which is good.  I think it could maybe stand to
be a little further along in the process (like, maybe have one
corner nearly complete and get increasingly "raw" as you
move toward the opposite end of the level), but maybe that's
just me.  Also, I'm not sure how easy that would be to implement
if the level's to have any randomness to it at all, and on the
whole (from a gameplay perspective, especially as pertains to
replayability) keeping some randomness in tact is probably more
important than superficial aesthetics.

The bottom level was initially almost empty of monsters, but by
the time I finished dealing with the warden some had shown up.
The architecture was sufficiently interesting.  The dialog for
the warden could probably stand to be worked on some more.

As I said before, I can't really speak to difficulty, since I used
wizard mode to reach the quest in the first place.  If I ever get
enough of a grip on the role to get to the quest in a normal game,
I'll probably have more to say then, but that could be a while.


